When you create a new component (application, data store, or shared infrastructure), follow this workflow.

## Step 1: Create a new GitHub repository

{% include github-repo.html %}

After completing runtime-specific setup, return to this page and continue with the common steps below.

If you are creating infrastructure-only components, skip this step and go straight to the common workflow.

## Step 2: Set up repository and CI/CD

1. [Add the repository to Jenkins](jenkins-repository.html)
2. [Add a Helm chart](helm-chart.html) for deployable services
3. [Configure GitOps with Flux](gitops-flux.html#application-config-in-flux)

## Step 3: Set up infrastructure

[Add infrastructure as code](infrastructure-as-code.html) where infrastructure is required

## Step 4: Configure security

1. [Set up secrets management](secrets-management.html)
2. [Configure TLS certificates](tls-certificates.html)

## Step 5: Configure networking

1. [Configure load balancer](load-balancer-configuration.html) for backend services
2. [Configure Public DNS](public-dns.html)
3. [Configure Front Door](front-door.html) for frontend services

## Step 6: Release management

Use [feature flags](feature-flags.html) to safely release changes

